                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesAsSectionsOf2Bundles"} As 2-sections of 2-bundles
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em twisted principal-bundle
            is the object classified by a cocycle in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            the way an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            is the object classified by a cocycle in plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            (generally in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            is classified in degree 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooped
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \hat G
          %p
            Given a realization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            as an abelian extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \to \hat G \to G
          %p
            of groups, i.e. given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}A \to \mathbf{B}\hat G \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
            is once
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} deloopable
            so that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
            continues to the right at least one step as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}\hat G \to \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^2 A
          %p
            the general mechanism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            induces a notion of
            %em twisted
            = succeed "-cohomology." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            = succeed "-bundles." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We give a discussion of twisted bundles as a realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            as described in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos#TwistedCohomology"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos – twisted cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETop%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ETop∞Grpd
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            this reproduces the traditional notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topological
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth
            twisted bundles, respectively, whose twists are correspondingly topological or smooth
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle"} circle n-bundle
          %h3#Setup Setup
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n-1}U(1) \in \mathbf{H}
            be the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle n-group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %p
            Fix once and for all an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in \mathbf{H}
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
          %p
            representing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\mathbf{c}] \in H_{Smooth}^2(\mathbf{B}G,U(1))
          %p
            Notice that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = P U(n)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+unitary+group"} projective unitary group
            in some dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/smooth%20infinity-groupoid#CohomologyOfLieGroups"} this theorem
            we have that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_{Smooth}^2(\mathbf{B}G, U(1)) \simeq H^3(B G, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#the_abstract_definition The abstract definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
            be as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Setup"} above
          #TheGroupExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}\hat G \to \mathbf{B}G \stackrel{\mathbf{c}}{\to} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
          %p
            This identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by the 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
          #TheGroupExtensionAsACircleBundle.num_note
            %h6#note Note
            %p Equivalently this means that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
