          %p (…)
          %h3#twisted_ktheory Twisted K-theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} Equivalence classes
            of twisted
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            = succeed "-twist" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            form a model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+bundle"} Chan-Paton bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+spin+structure"} twisted spin structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} twisted ∞-bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundle"} equivariant bundle
          %h2#References References
          %h3#GeneralReferences General
          %p
            The concept of twisted vector bundles was introduced, as a model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            (in the generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundles"} equivariant bundles
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+K-theory"} orbifold K-theory
          %ul
            %li#LupercioUribe01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernesto+Lupercio"}> Ernesto Lupercio
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gerbes over Orbifolds and Twisted K-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105039"} arXiv:math/0105039
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-003-1035-x"} doi:10.1007/s00220-003-1035-x
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-incarnation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LupercioUribe01"} Lupercio &amp; Uribe 2001, Def. 7.2.1
          %ul
            %li#Mackaay03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Mackaay"}> Marco Mackaay
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on the holonomy of connections in twisted bundles
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0106019"} arXiv:math/0106019
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=CTGDC_2003__44_1_39_0"} numdam:CTGDC_2003__44_1_39_0
          %p
            An equivalent characterization of twisted vector bundles (identified in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LupercioUribe01"} Lupercio &amp; Uribe 2001, (v2-) Prop. 7.2.2
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe+module"} bundle gerbe module
            in:
          %ul
            %li#BCMMS02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bouwknegt"}> Peter Bouwknegt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"} Alan Carey
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"} Michael Murray
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              %em K-theory of bundle gerbes and twisted K-theory
              , Commun Math Phys, 228 (2002) 17-49 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0106194"}> arXiv:hep-th/0106194
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002200200646"} doi:10.1007/s002200200646
          %p
            Discussion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
            for twisted vector bundles (phrased in terms of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe+modules"} gerbe modules
          %ul
            %li#Tomoda07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atsushi+Tomoda"}> Atsushi Tomoda
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the splitting principle of bundle gerbe modules
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ojm/1174324334"} Euclid
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ton.prosou.nu/official/ryousi2005.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#in_twisted_ktheory In twisted K-theory
          %p
            Just as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            model cocycles in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#LupercioUribe01"} Lupercio &amp; Uribe 2001
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BCMMS02"} BCMMS 2002
          %p
            The generalization of this construction to non-torsion twists requires using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vectorial+bundles"} vectorial bundles
            instead of plain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"}> Kiyonori Gomi
              , p. 7 of
              %em Twisted K-theory and finite-dimensional approximation
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0803.2327"}> arXiv:0803.2327
              )
          %p Then there is
          %ul
            %li#Karoubi
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted bundles and twisted K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~karoubi/Publications/89.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Pennig
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Pennig"}> Ulrich Pennig
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Twisted K-theory with coefficients in
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.4096"} arXiv:1103.4096
          %h3#ReferencesAsSectionsOf2Bundles As 2-sections of 2-bundles
          %p
            The observation that twisted vector bundles may be understood as higher-order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-vector+bundle"} 2-vector bundle
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            appears in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em Quantum 2-States: Sections of 2-vector bundles
              Talk at
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher categories and their applications
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Schreiber2States.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A discussion of this with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} 2-connections
            taken into account is in section 4.4.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              %em Connections on non-abelian Gerbes and their Holonomy
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1923"}> arXiv:0808.1923
              )
          %p
            A discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundles"} principal infinity-bundles
            (as opposed to higher vector bundles), is in section “2.3.5 Twisted cohomology and sections” and then in section “3.3.7.2 Twisted 1-bundles – twisted K-theory”
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p The observation then re-appears independently in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher geometric quantization
              %em Higher Structures
              in Göttingen (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.crcg.de/wiki/Higher_geometric_quantization"}> pdf slides
              )
